    <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">A dairy kitchen is a social facility in former-USSR countries that provides free dairy food for certain groups of people, defined by local regulations. May include newborn babies, pregnant women, feeding mothers, toddlers.</skos:scopeNote>
